<p style="text-align: center;"><img src="/images/2014/Barn-Cat-3.jpg" alt="A painting of a barn cat sitting in a driveway in front of a large white barn." width="400" height="527" /></p>
<p style="text-align: center;">Barn Cat. 12" x 9", oil on linen panel. 2014</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">I came across this cat at Oakland Green farm while plein air painting in the early fall. She just happened to be sitting in the way when I was taking photos of one of the barns. &nbsp;I played around with the composition slightly, especially the foreground shadows which originally went all the way across the foreground.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">It was difficult to stop myself from over painting this scene. &nbsp;It took a lot of effort to walk away, yet I still went back the next day and reworked the barn doors.</p>